@ Index:   Integrand cos(x·sin t) for integration
@ Author:  Hewlett-Packard, Walter Bonin
@ Created: 1979-05-01 by HP, original OM publication date unknown
@ Version: 0.29
@ Tested:  Requires RAD mode
@ Input:   Variables x=1 and t={0, 𝜋/2}
@ Output:  Stack X = {1, 0.5403023058681397174009366074429766} for those t inputs
@
@ Computes cos(𝑥⋅sin(𝑡)) with the variables given via menu input,
@ with the intention that this function then be integrated.
@
@ Based on the HP-34C _Owner's Handbook and Programming Guide_ Bessel
@ function examples starting on p.202, enhanced with MVAR for the
@ "Interactive Integrating Expressions Stored in Programs" section of
@ the WP43 Owner's Manual.  The version number above is for the latest
@ publication we checked of the OM.
LBL ‘IBessI’
  MVAR ‘x’
  MVAR ‘t’
  RCL ‘t’
  sin(𝑥)
  RCL× ‘x’
  cos(𝑥)
  RTN
  END
.END.
